==Reception==
''Justice League Unlimited'' received critical acclaim and is listed as one of the best animated television shows of all time. [[IGN]] named ''Justice League/Justice League Unlimited'' as the 20th best animated television series of all time.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.ign.com/lists/top-100-animated-series/20|title = Top 1000 Animated Series - IGN.com}}</ref> Similarly, [[IndieWire]] also ranked the series as the 20th best animated show of all time.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.indiewire.com/feature/best-animated-series-all-time-cartoons-anime-tv-1202021835/5/ | title=The Best Animated Series of All Time | date=4 March 2022 }}</ref> James Whitbrook, editor of [[io9]], wrote "''Justice League Unlimited'' is simply the greatest superhero show of all time", further stating "it embraced its source material wholly, and was unafraid to be the wildest, biggest, comic-book-iest show it could be."<ref>{{cite web | url=https://gizmodo.com/why-justice-league-unlimited-was-and-still-is-the-bes-1742256265 | title=Why Justice League Unlimited Was, and Still is, the Best Superhero TV Show | date=13 November 2015 }}</ref> Producer Bruce Timm has stated that amongst all the shows he has worked on, this show is his favorite.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.denofgeek.com/tv/bruce-timm-interview-justice-league-batman-harley-quinn-more/ | title=Bruce Timm Interview: Justice League, Batman, Harley Quinn, & More | date=8 June 2015 }}</ref>

